WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.296
With thirty-three elements and thirty-two

00:00:02.296 --> 00:00:04.450
threads per block, main launches two

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.964
blocks. Each thread needs to work out

00:00:06.964 --> 00:00:09.119
which array index belongs to it.

00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:13.553
CUDA grid of one returns the index across

00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:16.121
all blocks. Multiply the block number by

00:00:16.121 --> 00:00:19.056
the threads per block and add the thread

00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:21.623
number. Block one, thread zero gets index

00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:21.990
thirty-two.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.579
Index thirty-two is the last valid

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:27.321
position. The next thread gets

00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:29.410
thirty-three and skips the reads and

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.848
write. Put both indices into the kernel's

00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:34.285
bounds check to see which thread enters

00:00:34.285 --> 00:00:35.330
the if block.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.776
In main, change the launch to three blocks

00:00:39.776 --> 00:00:42.354
of sixteen threads each. Block two, thread

00:00:42.354 --> 00:00:44.932
zero writes the same array position. The

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:47.142
diagnostic print in the notebook shows

00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:49.352
that thread's block and thread numbers.
